---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Zcompressor vs PDF2Go - Secure Ad-Free PDF2Go Alternative | Compress PDF"
  description="Compare Zcompressor and PDF2Go. Learn why Zcompressor is a faster, more secure, and completely ad-free alternative to PDF2Go, processing PDFs 100% locally."
  ogUrl="https://zcompressor.com/vs/pdf2go"
>
  <!-- JSON-LD FAQ Schema for SEO -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does Zcompressor compare to PDF2Go?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>PDF2Go uploads your files to external cloud servers and serves heavy visual advertising to free users, while restricting batch sizes. Zcompressor is 100% free, processes documents locally inside your browser (no server uploads), and is completely ad-free.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why is Zcompressor faster than PDF2Go for large files?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>With PDF2Go, you must wait for your file to upload to their server, wait in a processing queue, and then download the output. Zcompressor compresses documents locally in browser RAM, eliminating network upload latency entirely and speeding up the process for large PDFs.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is my data safer on Zcompressor than on PDF2Go?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Because Zcompressor utilizes local client-side processing, your documents never traverse the web or reside on third-party servers. This protects your sensitive business, medical, or legal documents from external exposure.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <Header />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas-soft text-ink py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto">
      <!-- Eyebrow & Title -->
      <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
        <span
          class="text-caption-mono font-mono text-link-deep dark:text-cyan-deep uppercase tracking-wider block mb-3 animate-fade-in"
        >
          Security Review
        </span>
        <h1
          class="text-display-lg md:text-display-xl text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-1.5px] md:tracking-[-2.4px] mb-4"
        >
          Zcompressor vs PDF2Go.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-body-lg text-body text-balance">
          A security and speed comparison between local browser compilation and ad-supported cloud upload tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview Section -->
      <section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
          PDF2Go is a multi-utility online document converter. However, to sustain its free tier, PDF2Go serves aggressive display ads, limits maximum file sizes, and requires all files to be uploaded to remote cloud networks.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
          Zcompressor offers an elegant developer-platform aesthetic, focusing solely on high-speed, local client-side PDF compression without advertisements or paywalls.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Side-by-Side Comparison Table -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.96px] mb-6">
          Feature Breakdown.
        </h2>
        <div class="border border-hairline rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-level-2 bg-canvas">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-mute uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Feature</th>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-ink font-semibold uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Zcompressor</th>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-mute uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">PDF2Go</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Advertising & Clutter</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">100% Ad-Free</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Heavy display ads & redirects</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Upload Dependency</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">None (Processes in local RAM)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Required (Transfers file to cloud)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Privacy Controls</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Files never leave your device</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Files stored on external servers</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Batch Conversions</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Unlimited concurrent batching</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Limited on free tier</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">User Flow Friction</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Frictionless (No login required)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Frequent popups promoting upgrades</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Deep Dive Comparisons -->
      <section class="space-y-10 mb-16">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] mb-3">
            Bypass heavy advertising and layout clutter.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
            PDF2Go’s interface is saturated with visual banner advertising, auto-playing media, and conversion countdown timers. This not only clutters your workspace but also slows down browser rendering speeds and increases bandwidth usage.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
            Zcompressor uses a minimalist developer dashboard style. The clean, dark-mode-ready interface features absolutely no advertisements, letting you focus on the document optimization task efficiently.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-lg bg-canvas border border-hairline p-6 shadow-level-3">
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] mb-3">
            Instant local thread execution.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Cloud processing systems like PDF2Go must partition processing power between thousands of concurrent users. Free users are queued, resulting in sluggish processing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
            Zcompressor compiles its compression engines into standard WebAssembly and JavaScript running inside local web workers. By executing tasks locally on your device, you get instant feedback and maximum speed without shared queue delays.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12 mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.96px] mb-8">
          Frequently Asked Questions.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Can Zcompressor compress PDFs without an internet connection?</h4>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Yes. Once Zcompressor is loaded in your browser, all PDF optimization takes place offline inside your browser sandbox. PDF2Go will fail completely without an active internet connection.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Are there any file size limits?</h4>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Zcompressor does not enforce arbitrary upload caps. Your files are limited only by the local RAM allocated to your browser tab, making it highly effective for bulk processing documents.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Call to Action -->
      <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold mb-6">Try fast, secure, ad-free PDF compression.</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="/compress-pdf"
            class="px-6 h-[48px] bg-primary text-on-primary text-button-lg rounded-pill hover:bg-black transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center shadow-level-3 hover:scale-[1.02] duration-200"
          >
            Start Compressing
          </a>
          <a
            href="/vs"
            class="px-6 h-[48px] bg-canvas text-ink border border-hairline text-button-lg rounded-pill hover:bg-canvas-soft transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center shadow-level-2 hover:scale-[1.02] duration-200"
          >
            View Alternatives
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
